# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing in this block may ever be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# dbt writes credentials into profiles.yml when you run `dbt init`.
# This project keeps its own profiles.yml under dbt/ and reads every secret
# through env_var(), so the file below is only the interactive-init leftover.
.dbt/
profiles.yml
!dbt/profiles.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dbt build artefacts. Regenerated by `dbt run`; never source of truth.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dbt/target/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded and derived data.
#
# Rule of thumb for this repo: if a file regenerates from a documented source
# by running a script, it does not belong in git. `data/` is the landing zone
# for everything fetched at runtime.
#
# Specifically excluded:
#   - APCIQ quarterly PDFs: licence forbids redistributing the data as such
#     (docs/data-sources.md section 2.2). ~200 MB for 29 quarters.
#   - MAMH roll extract: 52.5 MB, regenerates in 88 s from a CC-BY source
#     (docs/data-sources.md section 2.8).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written as data/* rather than data/ so that ONE file inside it can be tracked:
# data/.gitkeep. The runner container mounts a writable directory at /app/data,
# inside a repository that is bind-mounted read-only -- and Docker cannot create
# a mount point in a read-only filesystem. The directory has to arrive with the
# deployed code, which means git has to carry it. Everything in it is still
# ignored, and data/apciq/ never even gets walked.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
*.pdf
mamh_roll_*_island.csv

# sample_data/ IS committed on purpose: small, real extracts that let a reader
# check the Data Source Matrix without downloading anything. Guard against a
# large file landing there by accident.
sample_data/**/*.zip
sample_data/**/*.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Power BI
#
# A Power BI Project (.pbip) splits into a DEFINITION -- tables, relationships,
# DAX measures, pages, visuals, all plain text -- and a DATA CACHE. Only the
# definition belongs here. The cache is a full copy of every row loaded in
# Import mode, and this model loads APCIQ figures, whose licence (page 65 of
# every edition) forbids reproduction "en tout ou en partie, directement ou
# indirectement".
#
# Microsoft's own default .gitignore for PBIP excludes exactly these two files.
# Power BI Desktop writes that file ONLY if no .gitignore exists in the folder
# or in the parent repository -- this repository has one, so Desktop will write
# nothing and these lines are the only thing standing between the cache and a
# commit. Verified on learn.microsoft.com, page dated 2026-08-18.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.pbi/cache.abf
**/.pbi/localSettings.json

# A .pbix, unlike a .pbip, carries its data inside the file with no way to
# separate it, and compressed, so no secret scanner can look in (demonstrated
# by a failed positive control on 2026-08-22). Ignored by default so that
# committing one has to be a decision. The exception below is the J2 report,
# committed knowingly: it holds Bank of Canada rates, which are public.
*.pbix
!powerbi/mhi_interest_rates.pbix
